add('THE PRODUCT EXPERIENCE','One service. One intent.<br><em>A plan generated for this run.</em>',f'''
<div class="product-board"><div class="board-top"><span><b>payments-api</b> / staging</span>{tag('CONCEPT WORKFLOW')}</div><div class="board-inputs"><div><small>01 / APPLICATION INTENT</small><h3>Publish an image.<br>Deliver to staging.</h3><p>Native project: Node.js + locked dependencies</p>{tool('nodedotjs','Node.js')}{tool('docker','Container')}</div><div><small>02 / EFFECTIVE POLICY</small><ul class="checks"><li>Approved runtime and package sources</li><li>Tests, coverage and security checks</li><li>SBOM + signed provenance</li><li>Authorized registry and staging target</li></ul></div></div><div class="board-plan"><small>03 / PROJECT + CONFIGURATION + POLICY → GENERATED PLAN · FROZEN BEFORE EXECUTION</small><div class="plan-nodes"><span>Capture<br><b>source</b></span><i>→</i><span>Prepare<br><b>inputs</b></span><i>→</i><span>Build<br><b>& test</b></span><i>→</i><span>Scan<br><b>& attest</b></span><i>→</i><span>Publish<br><b>artifact</b></span><i>→</i><span>Authorize<br><b>delivery</b></span></div></div></div>''',source='Product storyboard; not a screenshot of shipped managed functionality.',notes='Staging deployment is roadmap. Generated plan includes all destinations/gates up front; resulting artifact digests bind later. Board uses conceptual labels, not promised config/API schema.')

add('MANAGED ARTIFACT SECURITY','Verifiable evidence to production.<br><em>Without the infrastructure burden.</em>',f'''<div class="security-flow">{''.join('<div class="security-stage">'+ico(i)+'<h3>'+t+'</h3><p>'+d+'</p><div class="evidence-binding"><small>CONNECTED EVIDENCE</small><b>'+e+'</b></div></div>' for i,t,d,e in [('code','Source','Capture the revision and governing requirements.','Source + policy identity'),('graph','Build','Run approved tools and required security checks.','SBOM + signed provenance'),('package','Verified artifact','Bind results to exact bytes; verify before publication.','Digest + checks + receipt'),('launch','Production','Verify evidence and current authorization before deployment.','Release decision + audit trail')])}</div><div class="managed-service"><div>{ico('policy')}<h3>Oyzu operates the supporting services.</h3></div><p>Policy & identity · signing coordination · evidence storage & retention · verification & audit</p></div><div class="takeaway">Less security infrastructure to assemble, integrate and operate.</div>''',source='Managed product vision. Complete evidence, publication and deployment services are roadmap; current implementation appears on slide 11.',notes='Managed platform coordinates checks, signing, artifact-bound evidence and authorization. Customers retain their CI/registries and can bring security tools; no promise of zero customer infrastructure or automatic vulnerability elimination. Verification needs trusted producer identities, signatures, artifact digests and fresh assessments. Production gates are planned, not shipped.')

add('ONE GOVERNED DEVELOPER EXPERIENCE','One CLI. One configuration interface.<br><em>Everywhere software gets built.</em>',f'''
<div class="policy-band">{ico('code')}<div><small>OYZU CLI · NATIVE PROJECT FILES + DECLARED INTENT</small><b>Install approved tools. Apply policy. Execute the generated plan.</b></div></div><div class="distribution"><span>↓</span><span>↓</span><span>↓</span></div><div class="three contexts">{benefit('person','Developer machines','One entry point for governed tool installation, version selection and local builds.')}{benefit('agent','Cloud & AI agents','The same commands and configuration provision tools and execute automated work.')}{benefit('runner','Any CI system','A thin bootstrap invokes Oyzu; the same interface governs the build across runners.')}</div><div class="cli-foundation"><span>Approved toolchains</span><span>Policy distribution</span><span>Hermetic builds*</span><span>Connected evidence</span></div><div class="takeaway">Standardize how teams work without standardizing on one CI provider.</div>''',source='Target cross-environment experience. *Hermetic execution applies to qualified build environments; shims govern commands routed through Oyzu.',notes='One CLI and streamlined configuration interface retain native project manifests; this is not one replacement file for all ecosystems. The CLI and agent provide governed tool installation, version resolution, policy distribution and execution. Configuration declares intent while organizational policy sets authority. User experience is consistent across workstations, cloud agents and CI; supported capabilities vary by execution environment. Full managed governance is roadmap. Hermetic builds require qualified workers; ordinary local commands are not implicitly isolated. Endpoint controls remain necessary to prevent bypass.')

add('BETTER TOGETHER','Every action. Every artifact.<br><em>One connected audit trail.</em>',f'''
<div class="ecosystem-v2"><div class="eco-side"><div class="eco-group"><small>TRIGGERS & QUALIFIED RUNNERS</small><div>{tool('githubactions','GitHub Actions')}{tool('jenkins','Jenkins')}{tool('gitlab','GitLab')}</div></div><div class="eco-group"><small>NATIVE BUILD CAPABILITIES</small><div>{tool('nodedotjs','Node.js')}{tool('python','Python')}{tool('go','Go')}{tool('rust','Rust')}</div></div><div class="eco-group"><small>DATABASE CHANGES</small><div>{tool('liquibase','Liquibase')}{tool('flyway','Flyway')}</div></div></div><div class="eco-center"><div class="eco-link"></div><div class="eco-hub"><img src="logo-color.svg" alt="Oyzu"><p>Unified delivery record</p><small>ACTIONS • ARTIFACTS • STATUS</small></div><div class="eco-link"></div></div><div class="eco-side"><div class="eco-group"><small>CHECKS & ARTIFACT DESTINATIONS</small><div>{tool('snyk','Snyk')}{tool('jfrog','JFrog')}{tool('sonatype','Sonatype')}{tool('docker','Docker / OCI')}</div></div><div class="eco-group"><small>CLOUDS & DELIVERY CAPABILITIES</small><div class="delivery-targets">{tool('aws','AWS')}{tool('azure','Azure')}{tool('googlecloud','Google Cloud')}{tool('kubernetes','Kubernetes')}{tool('helm','Helm')}</div></div><div class="eco-group"><small>INFRASTRUCTURE & CONFIGURATION</small><div>{tool('ansible','Ansible')}{tool('terraform','Terraform')}<span class="tool"><img src="tool-logos/cloudformation.png" alt=""><span>CloudFormation</span></span></div></div></div></div><div class="audit-strip"><span><b>Know the artifact</b>Source · digest · SBOM</span><span><b>Verify the history</b>Actions · attestations · provenance</span><span><b>Explain the outcome</b>Policy decisions · status · deployments</span></div><div class="takeaway">Know what was built, how, why it could ship and where it went, all in one place.</div>''',source='Target audit experience across connected build and deployment systems. Evidence gaps stay visible. Logos show intended integrations, not partnerships.',notes='Unified record correlates action identity, artifact digests, execution status, attestations, provenance, policy decisions, publication receipts and deployment observations. Coverage depends on connected systems reporting events; missing evidence is explicit. Publication adapters must reuse connectors/leases. Qualified third-party capabilities can complement Oyzu; own workers/CD introduce additional direct competition later. Database migration and infrastructure tools are included in the intended governed lifecycle per founder scope; this diagram is not an implementation-conformance claim. Native profiles partial.')

add('THE COMPETITIVE CHOICE','The question is who maintains<br><em>the path to production.</em>',f'''
<table class="competition"><thead><tr><th>Approach</th><th>Existing strength</th><th>Oyzu’s proposed advantage</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b>CI + reusable workflows</b><small>GitHub Actions · Jenkins</small></td><td>Flexible execution and shared automation</td><td>Generate each execution plan from project facts, configuration and policy</td></tr><tr><td><b>Integrated delivery platforms</b><small>GitLab Auto DevOps · Harness</small></td><td>GitLab Auto DevOps detects projects and applies predefined CI/CD templates; Harness offers delivery governance</td><td>No application pipeline templates to maintain; shared policy from workstation through delivery</td></tr><tr><td><b>Programmable / opinionated builds</b><small>Dagger · Cloud Native Buildpacks</small></td><td>Portable pipelines or source-to-image conventions</td><td>Join native builds, publication authority and evidence in one governed lifecycle</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="comparison-bottom"><span><b>Direct overlap</b>Delivery orchestration and governance</span><span><b>Complementary</b>Runners, scanners, registries, native tools</span><span><b>Tradeoff</b>Opinionated support over arbitrary workflows</span></div>''',source='Sources and scope in appendix. Advantage is a thesis to demonstrate, not an exclusive-feature claim.',notes='GitLab Auto DevOps is close prior art, explicitly acknowledged. Harness governance source blocked in live retrieval; category statement is broad, not feature audit. GitHub reusable workflows, Dagger, CNB, GitLab Auto DevOps docs verified. No assertion of absent competitor capability. Measure configuration, migration time, exceptions and enforcement coverage.')

